  "scientific_limits": {
    "en": "Original low-poly folded oyster fossil form, historically called Lopha, informed by Actinostreon marshii. Unequal complete valves, broad attachment region, irregular radial folds and a geometric zigzag commissure. Historical Lopha name; Actinostreon marshii-informed art, not exact specimen replication. Pairing, depth, unseen geometry and color are inferred.",
    "zh": "历史名称 Lopha 的原创低多边形折缘牡蛎化石形态，参考 Actinostreon marshii：不等双壳、宽附着区、不规则放射褶与几何锯齿接缝。 沿用历史名称 Lopha，参考 Actinostreon marshii；非标本精确复刻，配壳、深度、不可见几何与颜色为推定。"
  },
